00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:50.520
{=3}Kamakura Dormitory

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:50.640
{=3}Kamakura Dormitory

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:50.770
{=3}Kamakura Dormitory

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:55.250
and conduct yourselves like
responsible high-schoolers.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.220
Okay, quiet down!

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.100
Look at this.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:10.600
It's National Route 134,
the Shonan Bullet Road!

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:23.430
"Enoshima"

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:15.400
It's near the inn where we'll be staying.
Want to go see it during our free time?

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:18.360
Just looking at a road isn't any fun.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.280
Okay, sure, maybe not,

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:23.620
but do you have something else
you're looking forward to doing?

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:28.160
Kozabuta ham, the fish dishes of Misaki,
and Kamakura's sweets.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:29.620
Food?

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:33.960
I've been saving a reserve fund from my
meager scholarship money every month,

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:37.210
so I need to let myself
splurge a little bit.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:42.680
Hmm. Well, maybe I'll go
and see it by myself.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:05.260
Trip Guide

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:05.260
Mukawa High School

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:05.260
Kamakura Dormitory

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:30.520
You're kidding me.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:35.100
Yes. I have a fever.

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:37.190
Yes.

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:40.110
I'll have to stay home.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:42.150
Yes.

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:44.070
Goodbye.

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:05.050
Are you kidding me?

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:11.390
- Hints -

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:11.390
1. Regarding clothing

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:11.390
(1) Wear your uniform properly.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:11.390
(2) Choose specified, comfortable shoes.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:11.390
2. What to prepare for the trip

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:19.250
Gym clothes count as a uniform.

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:23.960
There.

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:29.260
I could take the Koshu Highway
to National Route 137.

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:33.930
Then go up to Lake Sagami
and head south on Route 412.

00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:38.020
If I'm watching out for
lots of uphill climbs...

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:41.610
I guess I can't tell from this.

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:24.060
Off I go.

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:50.720
Good.

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:23.670
It sounds dangerous.
You probably shouldn't.

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:26.130
Is it really that dangerous?

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:28.880
If I tell you to stay put,
would you listen?

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:30.670
Hmm...

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:33.050
Maybe I'll listen next time.

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:38.510
You're really starting to think like
a biker, aren't you? All right.

00:08:38.510 --> 00:08:40.600
I won't say anything to the teacher,

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:43.390
but I will plead your case
with you when you do arrive.

00:08:43.390 --> 00:08:46.860
Be careful, okay? If something
seems questionable, stay away.

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:49.730
If anything happens, don't hesitate
to stop, then turn around.

00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:53.400
Mm-hmm. Thanks, Reiko.

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:45.580
Just under an hour and
a half to come this far...

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:48.710
If I head straight south from here,

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:52.340
I'll hit National Route 1 at Odawara
once I'm over the Hakone mountains.

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:55.090
I'll turn left there
and head for Kanagawa.

00:09:55.090 --> 00:09:57.800
From there it's Kamakura by way of Shonan.

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:00.550
I'll go left at the
Hagiwarakita intersection

00:10:00.550 --> 00:10:05.430
and take National Route 246.
It's kind of the long way around,

00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:08.270
but it's easier to get over
the mountains this way.

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:20.850
"School Excursion Itinerary 2"

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:21.030
17:00, huh?

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:30.670
Gotemba? Wow, you're making good time.

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:33.630
A little too good. I might arrive
at the inn ahead of you.

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:35.300
Hmm...

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:38.130
You know, there's nothing
to do if you get there early.

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:40.180
Why not enjoy your trip a little?

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:42.930
"Motorcycle parking"

00:10:40.180 --> 00:10:44.180
Oh, mm-hmm. Thanks.

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:02.220
Roadside Station Subashiri

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:36.500
{=6}Fuji Azami Line

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:08.830
Mt. Fuji 
Subashiri Trail

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:33.120
I'll let you off with just
this much for today.

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:30.430
Route 134.

00:13:30.430 --> 00:13:32.850
The Shonan Bullet Road.

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:08.820
Shonan Ohashi Bridge

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:31.850
Enoden Kamakurakokomae Station

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:20.290
I should probably get going.

00:15:58.250 --> 00:15:59.200
Huh?

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:01.000
What's the matter?

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:03.130
Hey, what's she doing here?

00:16:03.130 --> 00:16:05.420
I thought she was staying home.

00:16:16.850 --> 00:16:19.470
I'm glad you made it here.

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:20.810
Mm-hmm.

00:16:32.610 --> 00:16:36.700
Honestly, what would you have done
if you'd gotten into an accident?

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:40.410
Well, we can't exactly turn her away.

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:42.460
It goes without saying that
during the excursion,

00:16:42.460 --> 00:16:45.420
you are not allowed to ride your
motorbike. Is that understood?

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:48.590
Yes. I'm so sorry about this.

00:16:48.590 --> 00:16:50.550
Thank you very much.

00:16:50.550 --> 00:16:52.420
The important thing
is that nobody got hurt.

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:54.890
Yes, and she does appear to
be sorry for what she did.

00:16:54.890 --> 00:16:56.640
I suppose so.

00:16:58.310 --> 00:17:01.850
Aww, I'm exhausted.

00:17:04.730 --> 00:17:06.270
Thanks.

00:17:15.530 --> 00:17:16.950
Well?

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:23.790
Let's go hit the baths.

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:25.370
Let's go!

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:31.170
Well? Well?

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:33.510
I went up Mt. Fuji.

00:17:35.010 --> 00:17:38.640
Mm-hmm, Mt. Fuji. Oh, yeah?

00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:41.810
I had to drop down to first gear
before Station 4,

00:17:41.810 --> 00:17:45.440
and then managed to get
to Station 5 that way.

00:17:45.440 --> 00:17:50.070
The Cub's first gear is there to
climb any uphill slope in Japan.

00:17:50.070 --> 00:17:53.190
The story is that when you get up a tough
mountain road on an off-road bike,

00:17:53.190 --> 00:17:57.610
there'll be an old man there on his Cub,
picking wild vegetables.

00:17:57.610 --> 00:18:00.200
On steep roads like the ones
in Onomichi or Nagasaki,

00:18:00.200 --> 00:18:06.580
Cubs make deliveries every day to homes
past slopes that cars can't climb.

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:09.330
Cubs are superior, all right.

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:13.050
Of course they are. They're the best.

00:18:13.050 --> 00:18:17.340
Oh, that's right. I went down Route 134.

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:20.510
Huh? The Shonan Bullet Road? No fair!

00:18:20.510 --> 00:18:22.600
How could you go there before me?

00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:24.180
Early bird gets the worm.

00:18:24.180 --> 00:18:28.150
It's still not fair! You traitor! Jeez...

00:18:54.710 --> 00:18:58.130
Hey, you asleep?

00:18:58.130 --> 00:18:59.680
What is it?

00:19:01.600 --> 00:19:04.140
About our free time tomorrow...

00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:11.230
Let's go buy some souvenir
<i>kurumicco </i>candies.

00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:12.610
I hope we see some squirrels.

00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:14.570
That would be nice, huh?

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:21.160
Here it is.

00:19:28.660 --> 00:19:30.370
Why do you have that?

00:19:30.370 --> 00:19:33.170
You can never be too prepared.

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:23.340
We really do belong up in the mountains!

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:29.660
Kanazawa-
hakkei Station

00:20:39.320 --> 00:20:43.240
It looks like my Cub has had it.

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:46.280
The engine, the electricals,
and the suspension are all shot.

00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:49.830
What's more, the frame is cracked.

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:55.920
So... what are you going to do?

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:59.340
That's why I'm thinking
of buying a new Cub.

00:20:59.340 --> 00:21:02.930
Someone I know has a shop
with some CTs for sale.

00:21:02.930 --> 00:21:08.220
A CT is a Hunter Cub, right? The kind
of Cub that goes up mountain roads.

00:21:08.220 --> 00:21:11.980
That's right. They stopped
making them in 2012,

00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:15.350
and the remaining distributor's
inventory is all gone.

00:21:15.350 --> 00:21:17.900
They're still in demand even now overseas.

00:21:17.900 --> 00:21:19.570
They call them Farm Bikes,

00:21:19.570 --> 00:21:23.530
and they're the service vehicles
they use on farms with huge fields.

00:21:23.530 --> 00:21:26.030
There are newer models out.

00:21:26.030 --> 00:21:28.330
Do you think those
electronically controlled Cubs

00:21:28.330 --> 00:21:30.790
are any kind of successors to the CT line?

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:36.580
The era of the Cub being the world's
greatest Farm Bike is over.

00:21:40.880 --> 00:21:43.920
I just need to take good care of my Cub.

00:21:43.920 --> 00:21:47.800
Heh, well, of course. I mean, it's a Cub.

00:21:47.800 --> 00:21:51.350
I'm sure that even ten years from now,
you'll have no trouble finding parts.

00:21:51.350 --> 00:21:53.850
You'll be able to ride it forever.

00:21:53.850 --> 00:21:55.890
Do you think so?

00:22:05.360 --> 00:22:09.700
When you buy your Hunter Cub,
let me ride it, too.

00:22:09.700 --> 00:22:14.870
Once I get it broken in. I'm going
to ride the heck out of it until then.

00:22:18.380 --> 00:22:21.460
I wonder if, like Reiko says,
50 years from now,

00:22:21.460 --> 00:22:27.630
or 100 years from now,
Cubs will still be consistently running.

00:22:27.630 --> 00:22:32.680
I'm not going to change.
I don't want to change.

00:22:32.680 --> 00:22:38.600
I'm going to keep riding forever.
Together with my Super Cub.

